P3 (owner-approved 2026-10-18): backport of upstream LibreOffice's Calc data-provider
hardening onto 25.8.7.3. The fixes are on libreoffice-26-2 / 26-2-5 and were never
backported to 25-8. Applied in upstream history order:

  6cc778595b7a  sc: only build the supported data providers when loading a document
                (csv, html, xml only; any other provider name in the document is ignored)
  c3355f20dcd5  don't bother loading exotic protocols for document-supplied data
                (= 6b218b521d38 on libreoffice-26-2; sc/webservicelink, dataprovider,
                sqldataprovider hunks only -- the forms/xforms hunk is carried separately
                as a universal patch, since it touches every module)
  a7c32cc2519d  sc: check the host when fetching an external data range
  8b882d3e7bd0  put calc external data mappings under link update control
                (conflict in sc/source/ui/view/tabvwsh4.cxx resolved by keeping 25.8's
                DocumentLinkManager::hasDdeOrOleOrWebServiceLinks(), which 26-2 renamed
                hasExternalLinks(), and adding the new rDoc.HasDataProviderMappings())

Upstream's tests (sc/qa/...) are not included: the WASM build does not compile them.
Unconditional, like upstream.

